2. HOW MIGRATION ACTUALLY WORKS

    1. Sign in to Bitvex by
       typing the address
       yourself -> API
       Management.
    2. Create v2 keys, set
       permissions/rate
       limits, deploy.
    3. Revoke the v1 keys
       once traffic is on
       v2.

  The official migration
  never needs your existing
  key, secret, or any 2FA
  code - new keys are
  CREATED in the console,
  not derived from old
  ones.

  Bitvex will NEVER:
  - Ask you to provide
    your current API key
    + secret on any page
    (an API secret plus
    withdrawal permissions
    is account-takeover
    grade material; no
    "migration assistant"
    needs it, because
    keys are not
    transferable by
    design)
  - Ask for a 2FA code by
    email or to "batch
    re-verify" the
    withdrawal address
    book (address
    whitelists carry over
    automatically; any
    future single address
    change is confirmed
    via in-app 2FA and
    email, one address at
    a time)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as
    "bitvex-notify" or
    "bvex-secure"

3. WHAT IS REAL IN THIS
   NOTICE

  The May 22 retirement
  and the reduce-only
  halt are real (the
  changelog on the
  official notice page
  is the source of
  truth) - but the
  migration is a console
  self-service task
  taking about 10
  minutes, with no
  secrets, no codes,
  and no 72-hour email
  deadline.

4. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

